    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d382">

                <pb facs="0474" n="308" sameAs="frus:frus1917/pg308"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 818.00/84</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Minister Hale </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegrams]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-02-17T13:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 17, 1917—1 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your February 13, 5 p.m. By authorization of the President you are instructed to
                    inform Tinoco that even if he is elected he will not be given recognition by the
                    United States.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
